section
/-! # `H(A)` is countable when `A` is countable

A piecewise projective map with breakpoints in the countable set `P_A` is determined by its
finite set of real breakpoints together with one element of the countable group `SL(2, A)` for
each of the finitely many intervals between them; `G(A)` is generated by these maps. -/

